    ":question/id": "021d25c6-08db-5f20-a89b-110389d08e29",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "e-3224",
    ":question/problem": "What is the equation of the circle given below?\n\n![](images/79/79111226781bc9d3ea9c00e217b93b9661d1e70bdfbee688c555dd899cf3d80e.png)",
    ":question/worked-solution": "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^2 + (y-b)^2 = r^2.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(-1,1)$ and the radius of the circle is $r = 3.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & ={3}^{2} \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
  ":knowledge-point/id": "82d6988b-3220-578f-ba1c-cd86b9e3dbf9",
