      ":question/problem": "![](images/98/9839540667b095cec69ce6ea429aa99b129e90fee26c4adf1f25ffa6019d5067.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(-5,0)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=7.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {(x-(-5))}^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & ={7}^{2} \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =49.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
